{
  "_": [
    "NOTES-FROM-PLANNING.md entry 163 section 3. A person who shoots a 6.5 Creedmoor typed 6.5 and GroupLab offered .257,",
    "because 6.53 mm is the nearest diameter to 6.5. Names are matched before numbers now, from this table.",
    "",
    "Every cartridge here is confirmed at its diameter by BOTH sources below, read on 2026-09-24. A cartridge only one",
    "source lists is in 'pending' with the one it has, and is offered nowhere until a second is found, because the entry",
    "asked for every diameter to be verified against two independent published sources before it goes in. Where the two",
    "sources disagree, the family carries a note and a range, and the disagreement is recorded in docs/CALIBRES.md.",
    "",
    "Families are in the order a suggestion list shows them: the common ones first.",
    "",
    "A family shorthand never points at a held cartridge or at a trap: '7.62' could be 7.62x39, '5.56' and '8.6' are held, '25' could be .25 ACP at 0.251, and '9' could be anything from 9mm to 9.3.",
    "'.223' is not a name here: with its leading point it is a diameter, entry 163 section 3.1 rule 3, and 0.223 in is a real .22 LR figure in source A. '223' without the point is .223 Remington."
  ],
  "sources": {
    "A": "Wikipedia, Table of handgun and rifle cartridges, bullet diameter column, which cites SAAMI and CIP. Read 2026-09-24.",
    "B": "Nosler load data, caliber and cartridge index, which lists each cartridge under its bullet diameter from the bullet maker's own load development. Read 2026-09-24."
  },
